{{!-- A2, "split hero" on Membership: the headline beside the standfirst, ruled off below.

	{{> "membership/hero-split" eyebrow=(t "Membership")}}     called from inside {{#post}}

	eyebrow   the theme's word for what kind of Surface this is

Unlike About's split hero this one carries no photograph — the design sets two columns of type
and nothing else, which is also why it needs no `{{#if feature_image}}`. `items-end` is what puts
the standfirst's last line on the headline's baseline. --}}
{{#if @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
	<section
		aria-labelledby="mem-h2"
		class="border-border border-b">
		<div class="container py-18">
			<p class="font-meta text-meta text-accent tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">{{eyebrow}}</p>

			<div class="mt-[22px] grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(300px,100%),1fr))] items-end gap-12">
				<h1
					id="mem-h2"
					class="font-display tracking-display max-w-[18ch] text-[clamp(34px,4.8vw,58px)] leading-[1.03] font-medium text-balance">{{title}}</h1>

				{{!-- `custom_excerpt`, not `{{excerpt}}` — same reason as About's opener: the
				Membership Surface prints `{{content}}` too, so the fifty-word fallback would set the
				body's own opening above it. See centered-intro.hbs. --}}
				{{#if custom_excerpt}}
					<p class="text-lead text-muted max-w-[48ch] leading-[1.55] text-pretty">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{{/if}}
